SUMMARY:TWO RIVERS CHAMBER ORCHESTRA - DOUBLES ANYONE?
LOCATION:Shepherdstown Presbyterian Church, Shepherdstown, WV
DESCRIPTION:Single Tickets: $40\nOsvaldo Golijov (Born 1960) — Last Round\nJohann Sebastian Bach (1685-1750) — Concerto for two violins in D minor\, Heather Austin-Stone\, violin\nSalvatore Amadeo\, violin\, Antonin Dvorak (1841-1904) —Serenade for Strings\, Op. 22\nThis concert begins with a fiery homage by Argentine composer Osvaldo Golijov to tango legend Astor Piazzolla\, written for double string quartet with a bass added as arbiter. The program continues with Bach’s beloved concerto for two violins\, whose three movements move from haunting to uplifting to vigorous. We close the concert and our season with Dvořák’s Serenade for Strings\, a richly romantic work for string orchestra.\nRESERVATIONS & TICKETS: MAY 30\, 2026 RESERVATIONS & TICKETS: MAY 31\, 2026\n
CATEGORIES:Music & Film & Stage
ORGANIZATION:Friends of Music
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SOURCE:friendswv.org/
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
